    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"auto\"><div>Noelia--</div><div>     You probably need to do  a bit of reading on structural equation modeling.  Degrees of freedom for the chi-square statistic is not affected by sample size, but rather by the number of observed variables (and the number of free parameters).</div><div>     Yes, the values under &quot;Estimator&quot; in the lavaan output are the values for your model.</div><div>     Your sample sizes are rather small for such a model, so the chi-square statistic is probably under-powered.</div><div>--Ed Rigdon<br><br>Sent from my iPad</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
